<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38285" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπᾰρᾰρίσκω</span></b> , aor. 1
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῆρσα</span>: aor. 2
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήρᾰρον</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fit to</i> or <i>upon, fasten,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύρας σταθμοῖσιν ἐπῆρσεν</span>
			<i>on</i> or <i>to</i> the posts, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.167
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ δὲ ζυγὸν ἤραρεν ἀμφοῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					50
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr. in 
				Ion.
			
			pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπάρηρα [ᾰρ</span>], plpf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπᾰρήρειν</span>:—<i>fit
				tight</i> or <i>exactly,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μία δὲ κληῒ ἐπαρήρει</span> a
			cross-bolt <i>was fitted therein,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.456
			</span></i>; part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαρηρώς, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υῖα</span>,
					<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ός</span>,</span>
			<i>close-fitting, well fixed,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖ ἐπαρηρὼς ποσσίν</span>
			<i>firm on</i> his feet, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				83
			</span></i>: also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπάρμενος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span>
			
				Ep.
			
			aor.
			part.
			
				Pass.
			, <i>well-fitted, prepared, ready,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίον, ὅπλα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				601
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				627
			</span></i>:—also in form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφάρμ-,</span>
			<i>suited,</i> c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				12.35
			</span></i>.</div>
